Campfire for BEAM, Android only: let the beam-wallet CLI build without asset swap.

Campfire runs beam-wallet on Android for create/restore (ProcessHost.initWallet runs
`beam-wallet restore`; wallet-api cannot create a wallet.db). Android forces
BEAM_ASSET_SWAP_SUPPORT off (CMakeLists.txt, ANDROID branch), and at tag
beam-7.5.14493 wallet/cli/cli.cpp guards the asset-swap command TABLE entries with
#ifdef BEAM_ASSET_SWAP_SUPPORT but not the functions they name (AssetsSwapList,
AssetSwapCreate, AssetSwapCancel, AssetSwapAccept), so the CLI does not compile
there ("use of undeclared identifier 'DexBoard'"). This wraps those functions in the
same #ifdef. With asset swap on nothing changes.

Android only: applied by scripts/beam/core/android/build_wallet_api.sh after the core
series (patches/0001-0005), never by the desktop builds. It adds lines to cli.cpp, and
in the shared series it would shift __LINE__ in the desktop beam-wallet and break its
pinned hashes. wallet-api does not compile cli.cpp; its Android build is byte-identical
with and without this patch. patch -p1.

--- a/wallet/cli/cli.cpp
+++ b/wallet/cli/cli.cpp
@@ -3006,6 +3006,7 @@
             });
     }
 
+#ifdef BEAM_ASSET_SWAP_SUPPORT  // Campfire: Android builds the CLI without asset swap
     int AssetsSwapList(const po::variables_map& vm)
     {
         CheckAssetsAllowed(vm);
@@ -3326,6 +3327,7 @@
 
         return 1;
     }
+#endif  // BEAM_ASSET_SWAP_SUPPORT
 }  // namespace
 
 io::Reactor::Ptr reactor;
